3:Scope: design decisions extracted verbatim-faithful from written sources, for a later engineering spec. Facts only, no synthesis. Status legend: CANON = fixed in TNS65-PARADIGM.md; PLAN = plan/support doc (not yet canon); UI = made UI decision (interface/ decision bank); STALE = source contradicted by canon; OPEN = open question/fork. Russian terms (Пила, Ткач, Челнок, Селектор, Цензор, Редактор, Труппа, Толмач, Паганель, Гефест, Пифия, анкета, варка, оседание, and similar) are quoted as literal bytes.
14:- **R-008 | p.14 roles, not model names** — canon fixes roles/interfaces/requirements; current composition (BGE-M3 on :5002, local 3B станок, pack lemmatizer) = replaceable implementation. Lemmatizer = deterministic dictionary service (RU pack = pymorphy3, MIT), ~100 MB resident, ms per replica, stdio/JSON contract (lemma, POS, tags), negation «не» = separate lemma. Ткач and Редактор prose = uncensored and/or literary-tuned model, external loop (CPU: 4 cores, no GPU, ceiling ~3B q4). Deep parse of first replica = one cheap LLM call per chapter. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:28–36. Status: CANON.
18:- **R-012 | p.20 three databases** — base.db = engine DB in engine folder, shipped by developer, read-only for живой ход, stores base narratives (global book scenarios, p.21). literary.db = world DB in world folder, point заготовки (names, time, style, dramaturgy nuances), filled by Forge, оседание goes there. world(name).db = operational world DB created at world birth, filled by player + engine; all game (collisions, events) + пачка персонажей: 16 Jung psychotypes × 6 estates = 96 cards generated at birth under строй/экономика; new character for a required arc + Пифия score is added by Forge in pause (p.7, step 3); in the live turn a character is born without history (p.12). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:46–48. Status: CANON.
19:- **R-013 | DB rights and priority** — живой ход writes only world(name).db, reads world(name).db + bank pools from literary.db, base.db read-only; on fact conflicts the world wins; Паганель writes world(name).db and never touches literary.db (p.16). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:50. Status: CANON.
23:- **R-017 | Admin UI map (part I)** — UI split player/admin, admin hidden from players. Sections: Миры (worlds) — list + анкета creation (p.13), button «начать новую жизнь» opens book in chosen world; Конфигурация мира (world-config) — анкета by tabs: описание, роли, статистика, рождение, граф, аудит; Чат (index) — живой ход: replica field, tabs мир/герой/система, service commands, «Моя книга» window (p.13); Роли (agents) — slot per role: provider, model, temperature, prompts, priority; Провайдеры (providers) — keys, call limits, models; Модели (models) — manager; Дашборд (dashboard) — post-factum counters/online; Граф (graph) — relationship graph (player window) + craft (social graph, p.15); Консоль наполнения (mcp) — filling DBs (narratives base.db, source books + epoch reference p.16, literary templates, economy; catalog build/delexification/fact check/import tools p.18, p.20); Настройки (settings) — станок params: server, LLM+embedding slots, NPC memory (p.8), world luck, Паганель card with two toggles «включён» and «походы наружу» (p.16). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:64–77. Status: CANON.
25:- **R-019 | Naming rule in UI (owner 16.10)** — role names (Ткач, Челнок, Пила, Паганель etc.) = code-names, live in canon+code, never shown to player (direct literary associations like Паганель — Jules Verne don't fit other-genre worlds); player-facing names functional, without references; vocabulary-split precedent «дайджест» (player) vs «сводка» (мастерская); player name of the cartographer = «Прорисовка карты». Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:81. Status: CANON.
28:- **R-022 | p.13 world birth — анкета core 4 fields** — (1) Синопсис: what the book is about, both ends (e.g. slave → emperor) = book application strengthened by finale (hero arc anchor gets both ends); (2) Описание мира: geography, laws, economy — explicit input for Паганель (p.16) and Гефест (p.18) along with source books; (3) Рождение героя: description, starting stats/characteristics — start data for Пифия's player card (p.17) and состав пробуждения (part V); (4) Цензура 16+/18+: world rating — model/provider choice (presets p.14), language style, violence, profanity, sex; 18+ narrows external slots to uncensored models and layers onto forge censorship (p.4). Frame fixed before first replica; no ready live prose at birth. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:91–98. Status: CANON.
30:- **R-024 | UI анкета full composition (canon 16.10)** — semantic core of 4 fields expanded in UI, each field names its consumer: Заголовок мира (world list name); Описание мира (= core 2); Синопсис (заявка) (= core 1, optional, 1–3 sentences); Пролог (short backstory/opening scene; Паганель path recon works in the prologue p.16); Язык мира (pack choice p.14, first pack = Russian); Режим походов (земля мира): real / fictional / mixed (p.16), chosen explicitly, NOT derived from genres; Жанры: canonical list of ten — фэнтези, научная фантастика, современная проза (Fiction), LitRPG, хоррор, постапокалипсис, исторический, киберпанк, стимпанк, мифология (multi-select; consumer = Паганель genre insert p.16); Правила мира: line-per-rule «name: description» (consumers = world laws overriding the insert p.16); Социальный строй: one of eleven — нет, феодализм, демократия, анархия, теократия, коммунизм, капитализм, социализм, трайбализм, рабовладение, меркантилизм (consumers = пачка п.20 + social graph p.15); Экономические модификаторы: checkboxes золотой стандарт, серебряная экономика, бартер, командная экономика (consumers = economy heritage p.15 + пачка p.20); Магия: system description (consumers = world laws p.16 + resistance-to-foreign p.19); Рождение героя (= core 3): name optional (empty = random), hints (sex, race, origin), starting age; Isekai = replay in same world (past stay stays in world history, world-that-remembers, part V); Цензура 16+/18+ (= core 4; absent in old UI drafts, added at canon alignment 16.10). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:102–117. Status: CANON.
33:- **R-027 | Заявка книги (book application)** — short 1–3 sentence application written by the player (authorship from line one), skippable (book works without it); after several sessions engine proposes one from player patterns (p.10), player approves/edits. Stored as text + meaning vector (:5002, p.8); drift measurable as a number. Three applications: night ковка priority shifts toward заявка; gap «заявка ↔ accumulated book» shown to player in дайджест; finished-book annotation = rework of заявка with actual content. Hard boundary: заявка = selection criterion, not plan; chooses/edits nothing inside chapters; Селектор/Пила never lead to it (Пифия precedent p.17); drift = plot. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:123–129. Status: CANON.
34:- **R-028 | p.21 scenario frame (base narratives)** — anchor = global book scenario = narrative from base.db (e.g. Иосиф и братья). Start: at world birth anchor = narrative nearest to анкета synopsis by meaning vectors (:5002), no LLM. Drift: aggregate chapter-intent vector checked against anchor at night, chapter end; base.db narrative embeddings computed once at engine build, check = pure mechanics. Retention = exactly one hook: when drift exceeds threshold Селектор submits exactly one holding hook — ружьё (uncharged first, p.12) or one quest (= the «one soft nudge»); if the nudge fails, anchor follows the player, scenario switches to a new vector (Иосиф → Иов). Invisibility: anchor switch never shown. Consumers: current anchor feeds night ковка plan (p.7) and Пифия гороскоп (p.17). Executors: embeddings+drift check = code; hook + anchor switch = Селектор. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:131–145. Status: CANON.
38:- **R-032 | p.9 conveyor with precomputation** — replica cut into sentences by punctuation, vectorized + lemmatized synchronously (pack dictionary mechanics = milliseconds). Pre-path runs in parallel: intent hypothesis (pack lexicon), mood → Пила, scene frame assembled from mechanics (state, graph, physiology don't depend on player words), preselect: bank record or Ткач prompt pre-assembly. Slot binder closes placeholder tokens ([NPCname], [NPCrole], [PLACE] etc.) at preselect without LLM: choice by Труппа/пачка tags (geography, estate, sex), declension by pack lemmatizer + NPC card (gender, cases); binding stored in world(name).db, lives a scene or chapter; same token in two arcs of one chapter = different persons (binding-number comparison); Ткач gets prompt without tokens. Confirmation: dictionary (lemmas) doesn't contradict hypothesis AND vector supports it (second opinion, no single judge) → meaning fixed; work goes to model (prompt ready, generation starts immediately) or to ready DB record (incl. оседание). Control by whole-replica point (robust to sentence reorder), analysis per sentence. Стоп-кран: until confirmation pre-path only reads/prepares; on conflict dictionary beats vector. Courage handle: спокойный mode = deep parse of first replica (p.13) before big decisions; дерзкий mode = when lemmas and vector agree with margin, рутина commits immediately. Оседание record reused already-trusted (trust level set pre-write, p.10), no re-review. Early word vectors (web client, word boundary = space or sign, completed word vectorized at once) feed Пила and forge relevance (p.8-7); commit only after full confirmed replica; Telegram gives no per-letter stream (Bot API sends replica whole on Enter) and is chosen as the NAT-solving outbound channel; edited message = new replica (re-vectorize, same stop-kran). Web transport = cloudflared tunnel (outbound to Cloudflare edge, no public ports); WSS inside tunnel; WebRTC rejected (needs public signaling/TURN); principle: only outbound connections. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:194–212. Status: CANON.
41:- **R-035 | p.11 streaming underlay — player time = background time** — scene delivered to chat incrementally: instant заготовки (character description from book, action-hook) laid under while Ткач writes live fragments; long fragments diluted with descriptions/actions as emotional hooks; waiting hidden — player reads. Селектор (ex-Драматург) watches Пила and picks action type: quest via NPC, small incident («спустило колесо») or other; on NPC the character+description served instantly from book, speech generated after. Player's reply time (reads/thinks/writes) = background computation time: continuation generated, engine preselects answer branches — negative branch → instantly ready DB record, positive → live model answer. Unused branches not discarded: candidates for оседание via p.10 conveyor (авто-критик, trust level). Стоп-кран p.9 extends to branches: unconfirmed branch writes nothing to world. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:241–247. Status: CANON.
42:- **R-036 | p.12 Труппа — engine character machinery** — characters = actors of one Труппа under engine; not created per-quest forever: cheap stage entry, memory accumulation, maturation to big roles and exit (incl. death) by engine decision, not pre-written script. Рождение без истории: NPC appears instantly from book (archetype, voice, looks); backstory may be absent through the second обращение. Память реакций: world cheaply records per meeting what the player saw (hook left in player memory — world knows) and how they reacted (подал / прогнал / не заметил); next meeting reads it in the attitude band (mechanics, not generation). Отложенная тайна (Твен, Дюма): true role not fixed at birth; secret assigned later from «полотно тайн» pool (переодетый принц, беглый каторжник, агент фракции…) at dramaturgic benefit (player initiative or Пила peak); hard rule: new secret reinterprets, never contradicts shown facts — «мир не выдавал ложных фактов — мир не раскрывал полных». Флаги тайны: per secret two flags «намекать» and «раскрывать» (e.g. переодетый принц: намекать да, раскрывать нет до крючка); flags not changed live; change = Селектор распоряжение at planning (p.11). Чеховское ружьё как политика: everything shown = registered guns; Селектор looks for an uncharged gun before introducing new elements. Судьба без игрока: character may be found killed/dead (world lives independently) = hook to pity/repentance; труп нищего с королевским перстнем = ружьё и тайна одним элементом; mechanics = far-circle fate vectors (p.7), find reads ready DB state, never back-fills. Порог смерти: at hero health threshold (working value 2%) engine guarantees farewell scene (time for dialog and завещание); death = part of the loop, scene works as hook+arc; before threshold world never forces death. Правило игрока: world never declines use of an abandoned hook — player initiative to the нищий → Труппа picks up, up to assigning the secret right then. Разделение контроля: Цензура = dictionary + ban-lists, automatic, live, for everything live; library admission (оседание, ковка into bank pool, полотно тайн) = авто-критик of мастерская with trust levels (p.10); live improvisation waits for no checks; owner intervenes by распоряжение (выкинуть, понизить, повысить, workshop order) — right, not duty. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:249–269. Status: CANON.
44:- **R-038 | p.7 background ковка in pauses** — full «all at once» run cancelled: ковка only by relevance. Staged pause timer measures player silence on server, open stage sets allowed work weight: pause ≥10 min = light fast computations + next-turn prep (mechanics without prose: ковка plan, vectors, collisions, bank reads, prompt pre-assembly; 10 min give no margin for scene generation); pause >1 h = more complex ковка; pause >3 h = heavy computations. Заготовки = forge artifacts stored in DB until activation: Паганель recon, new NPC elaboration, existing NPC collisions, location descriptions, scenes to brewing Пила peaks, neutral next-chapter пробуждение; weight must match open stage. Work split into resumable steps in a queue; player return = unfinished work neither invades живой ход nor discarded — next step queued to next pause; continues from stop point; step = unit of planning from queueing; non-resumable work not queued. Four priorities: (1) next chapter пробуждение — highest, deadline morning (missed = live-turn fallback p.13); (2) scenes to nearest Пила peaks; (3) гороскоп events (p.17); (4) bank top-up — batch, last. Timing: day кует evening, night кует morning and tomorrow; far-made заготовка risks missing player's actual path; unneeded one deactivates до крючка or goes to оседание; far заготовка only with free queue. Demand 2–5 заготовки/day by construction (пробуждение + peak insurance + hooks); night window covers it even at a single pause. Deactivation: заготовка activates at need without generation; review and censorship pass before deactivation (review = авто-критик trust level p.10; censorship = dictionary p.4) — live turn gets an already-checked DB record; instant characters from book/bank pools appear without per-item review (censorship passed at ковка; live dictionary works). Player turn always priority over background ковка. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:278–305. Status: CANON.
46:- **R-040 | p.18 Гефест — background assembly executor** — role = forge master; name of the live TNS35 subsystem = Forge (forge/edge.ts, forge/paganel/client.ts; p.16). Products: bank pool records, переплавка of осевшие сцены into slot blanks (p.10), гороскопы by Пифия order (p.17). Book-ковка frame inherited whole with two changes: (1) fb2 input — TNS35 parser reads txt/md only, so fb2→text insert goes before it (fb2 = XML: title/chapters to metadata, body to existing chunker); (2) Цензор при ковке — TNS35 censor only in runtime (Big Six), not in forge: dictionary censorship at ковка output, before bank write (p.4, all pools) — bank cleaned once at ковка, not per turn. Гефест/Паганель/Пифия = three separate entities, no hierarchy, parallel/on-need; no single «горн»; each has own tools and budgets (Паганель budgets p.16). Two shops: кузня (мастерская: hard artifacts, result to DB) and ткацкая (сцена: Ткач writes live); boundary per p.2; ткацкий словарь (станок, Челнок, полотно, нити, пряжа) inviolable. Process word canon: «ковка»; «варка» = historical synonym; «запекание» = same process variant in Паганель context. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:307–320. Status: CANON.
47:- **R-041 | p.16 Паганель — purpose and scope** — land not pre-described whole: grows with the hero; Паганель keeps the map ahead of steps so player never hits «край листа». Responsibility = land only (places, paths, knownness); no drama (essence line is not a hook; Ткач sows hooks over ready land); world effectively unlimited by map; live loop free of geography computation; executor = мастерская resident (Forge), not live-turn agent. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:322–324. Status: CANON.
48:- **R-042 | Паганель three modes** — (1) при ковке (atlas stage): extracts places and paths from source book incl. implicit ones («к вечеру добрались до…») and world fields; (2) на пороге (forge edge): builds next ring between turns; two triggers — hero closer than 2 days' travel to the edge, or scene named a place beyond the edge (gap `edge_of_atlas`); never inside a turn; (3) разведка пути: the only point near the turn — in the prologue, before Ткач: cheap mechanical check without LLM (hero at edge? input names unknown place?); «no» = zero cost, «yes» = one targeted call, timeout ~30 s; missed = turn proceeds anyway (improvisation + gap), Паганель builds later; recon = accelerator, never the only path; turn never blocked. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:326–330. Status: CANON.
49:- **R-043 | Two build forms** — кольцо (ring) for wanderings (radius ≈ week of travel); коридор for a promised route in one go («от Иерихона до Александрии две недели»): anchor points, segments with time, stops (immediately deferred events); promised term = frame: day sum converges to promise, discrepancy = reserve for deception and storms; corridor cheaper and more integral than rings. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:332. Status: CANON.
50:- **R-044 | Поход modes and tool** — Паганель's tool = large external LLM on its own key. Travel mode set by explicit анкета field (p.13): real land / fictional / mixed; never auto-derived from genres (owner 16.10). Летописец: real worlds may go outward («Лондон есть Лондон, стоит где стоял»); Картограф вымысла: no outward — land from the book's voice; Штурман: returns precise direction (east, south-east; star course in science worlds); Смешанный: real canvas + book points on top, fictional embedded into real, never reverse. World laws may override insert text. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:334. Status: CANON.
52:- **R-046 | Паганель output schema** — places: name, one essence line «what it is and why the world needs it» without plots, owner, knownness, coordinates; paths: type (тракт/река/море), anchor points with coordinates, friction coefficient; mentioned people: name and «кто он», no more. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:338. Status: CANON.
56:- **R-050 | Паганель contract** — writes world(name).db (places/routes, provenance='paganel', status='draft'); draft immediately visible to runtime (= world state); literary.db never touched. Record lifecycle: draft → auto-check at next ковка/promotion (censor-mechanics: world check + dictionary censorship; promotion by code, not human) → baked; rejected goes to перековка. Ring log in UI; owner intervention = post-factum распоряжение. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:346. Status: CANON.
57:- **R-051 | Паганель budget and switches** — ~10 LLM calls per ring, ~3 per recon session (budgets separate, configurable). UI card has two toggles: «включён» (default off = zero external calls) and «походы наружу» (default no). Key stored only in the card — live loop physically has no access. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:348. Status: CANON.
58:- **R-052 | Паганель place in TNS65** — background ковка in pauses (p.7 incl. player sleep) + prefilter of оседание conveyor (p.10). World outbound paths = Паганель recon (normal, with permission and timeout) and external model slots — both by explicit owner choice of the станок (p.14); everything else stays in мастерская. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:350. Status: CANON.
59:- **R-053 | Паганель inheritance** — TNS35 implementation works (forge/edge.ts, forge/paganel/client.ts, forge/paganel/ui-card.ts, domain/paganel-prompts.ts; test paganel-edge.test.ts green) — code inherited, item sets its role and bounds. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:352. Status: CANON.
60:- **R-054 | p.17 Пифия — replica predictor** — purpose: world answer never lags the replica; Паганель reads land, Пифия reads player. Gathers the replica-work block spread across loops (psychotype p.6, mood p.8-2, intent p.9, player patterns p.10) into one role with one output artifact; implements p.11 «engine predicts branches». Two artifacts: карта игрока — long-lived DB profile (psychotype, mood, interests, habits, avoidance areas), accumulated at nights from patterns (p.10), lives months; гороскоп — per-scene release: answer branches (p.11: negative, positive, aside; negative → instant DB record, positive → assembled Ткач prompt), Пила forecast (p.6: эхо or контрапункт), topics = which bank segment to forge (p.8-7); lives until topic change, then reworked in мастерская. Two execution levels: мастерская (pauses/night) full run (player card + scene + Пила → гороскоп, ковка by relevance p.7); сцена (живой ход) mechanics only — early typing vectors (p.9) checked against гороскоп, match = ready branch served instantly, no generation on scene. Three limits: (1) advice not sentence — Селектор may ignore (Пила precedent p.6); гороскоп realized only if player came there themselves; (2) stop-kran: unconfirmed branch writes nothing; (3) miss not forced: replica outside forecast → branch not served, goes to оседание candidates (p.11). Censorship at ковка applies to гороскоп without exceptions (p.4). Гороскоп forged by Гефест on Пифия order (p.18). Inheritance: inputs alive in TNS35 (Jung profiler 14 metrics p.6, night pattern statistics p.10); item sets role and bounds, builds no new mechanics. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:354–371. Status: CANON.
61:- **R-055 | p.10 оседание of live scenes** — successful live scenes reworked into reusable bank records in DB; applies to experience too: session player patterns (bargaining style, topics pulled, avoided: mechanical stats + vector topics p.8) compacted at night into thread memory and ковка plan (p.7); experience = data not text: no per-item review, goes to night сводка. Only full live scenes passing live-turn checks (fact validator, dictionary censorship) оседают; рутина never оседает (already in bank). Cleaning: cuts engine-substituted values (names, things, prices, places) → slots; unremovable (pronouns, retelling) marked for авто-критик, verdict feeds trust level; original kept beside for checking. Semantic dedup rejects scenes duplicating an existing record's meaning per key. Trust level (ex-«утверждение») issued by fully mechanical conveyor: live checks → cleaning → dedup → авто-критик. Авто-критик = Гефест function in мастерская (small model, offline/night; no new entity), Паганель = prefilter (p.16). High (checks clean, like or no remarks) → record to all three consumer roles at once; low (авто-критик remarks, dislike-borderline) → only draft for Ткач, never straight to player. Three consumer roles (p.2 boundary intact): insurance on Ткач silence, middle stylization layer on flat segments, draft for Ткач in a similar moment; peak still live Ткач. Storage: literary.db of own world; between worlds only through Forge; storage priority = scarce keys of ковка plan (p.7) — оседание = third пряжа source beside book and станок. Owner sees no lists: осевшее visible post-factum in logs/UI, intervention = распоряжение (выкинуть/понизить/повысить = workshop order), right not duty. Лайк/дизлайк in chat: direct quality signal — лайк raises scene's оседание priority; дизлайк rejects. TNS35 roles inherited whole: likes nudge narrow literary parameters (clamp ±15%, step 0.02, neutral = no shift, NOT psychotype); dislike 1st in a row = soft regeneration of last scene, 2nd in a row = rollback to player's raw turn. Hybrid mapping: on рутина dislike = instant re-pick of another bank record, 0 LLM; «перепиши мягче» = Ткач instruction on deep path; dislike reason suggested by Пила/настроение (TNS35 had one hardcoded «слишком агрессивно»). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:373–389. Status: CANON.
63:- **R-057 | Jump rules** — up to a day: instant jump (near circle recomputed by jump, far circle lazy in мастерская by fate vectors p.7; replay p.15); circle discrepancies not masked — delivered as lagging news («вести в этом мире действительно идут неделями»). Over a day = workshop order, world state recomputed in pause. Пила doesn't grow on a jump (no replicas = no data); world faces advance their drift (p.19). Jump never empty: way stated briefly and factually (рутина, Челнок — «долго и без событий»), and by jump end (evening/night) world may serve a surprise: Ткач or DB заготовка (Пифия гороскоп p.17); not every jump (else fast-forward becomes an adventure-call button — «предчувствие» precedent). If player doesn't continue, Селектор hints a possible event or seeds a hook into next morning's пробуждение. Quiet stretch = convenient world move: player writes montage, world answers with event (p.19). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:400–402. Status: CANON.
67:- **R-061 | Редактор** — external model, batch mode, cheap tariff (built-in pipeline can't pull a 30–40k-token chapter: hours at ~5.6 tok/s; 3B weak in Russian orthography). Chapter cut into scenes of 2–4k tokens; punctuation sheet fixed (dash, «ёлочки», ellipsis). Edit format = MD: Редактор submits edit list (было → стало), never republishes whole text. After text processing Редактор generates chapter summary (5–6 sentences) in section `## Краткое содержание` — one request, one model. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:410. Status: CANON.
72:- **R-066 | Deep parse of first replica** — once per chapter (other replicas give mood only, p.6); one cheap LLM call (p.14), not a separate live-turn stage: latency hidden in пробуждение-reading window (branch 1) or answer-assembly window; per-word vectorization already in conveyor (p.9). JSON fields «намерение / план / предчувствие / незакрытая тема», each with quote from player's replica (not retelling); field below confidence threshold ignored. Fields go to Ткач facts and Пифия player card (p.17). Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:435. Status: CANON.
74:- **R-068 | «Моя книга» window** — modal window, text editor; player opens from menu and sees: Краткое содержание = дайджест of current chapter (5–6 sentences, generated by Редактор after text processing); tabs: Содержание (all chapters list, navigation), Глава (full edited text), Правки Цензора (what Редактор changed, what was rejected), Сырой лог (unedited session log, optional); editor mode: player edits errors in chapter text right in the window. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:439–443. Status: CANON.
76:- **R-070 | Эпилог** — practically standalone chapter, written by the player = the only pure-authorship chapter; player marks important/turning moments (scenes, chapters) = author marking of book peaks. Data consumers: оседание priorities (p.10), book assembly (contents + dramatis personae), annotation (заявка rework with actual content — part II block), regression sessions, Пифия prediction calibration (p.17) on following books. Source: TNS65-PARADIGM.md:447. Status: CANON.
85:- **R-076 | 01-PARADIGM = developer retelling** — canon retold with «что решили / довод / пример / кто исполняет» blocks; declares TNS65-PARADIGM.md the truth source on any conflict. Note: its six-part split differs from canon (гибрид → глубина/вектор/конвейер → оседание/стриминг → труппа/глава/книга → модели/наследие/мастерская → мир/базы/рамка) and p.7 sits in part five. Source: DOCS/01-PARADIGM.md:3–5, 225–261. Status: PLAN.
87:- **R-078 | Two contours** — живой ход: player → Telegram/WSS → facade :8000 → turn conveyor → Челнок (bank) or Ткач (model) → answer; latency units of seconds (рутина) / 30–60 s (пик); writes only world(name).db. Мастерская: silence → pause stages → forge queue; Гефест/Паганель/Пифия → literary.db + world(name).db; latency minutes–hours, night window 8 h. Source: DOCS/02-ARCHITECTURE.md:19–46. Status: PLAN.
88:- **R-079 | Role chain (Big-Six-style table)** — 13 roles with contour/artifact/item: Челнок (p.1,3), Ткач (p.1,2), Селектор ex-Драматург (p.11,21), Пила (p.6), Цензор живого хода (p.12), Паганель (p.16), Пифия (p.17), Гефест/Forge (p.18), Авто-критик = Гефест function (p.10), Цензор при варке (p.4,18), Редактор batch (p.13), Цензор правок batch (p.13), Толмач = pack-build one-time translation (p.4, removed from live turn). Ткацкий словарь inviolable (станок, челнок, полотно, нити, пряжа). Source: DOCS/02-ARCHITECTURE.md:69–93. Status: PLAN.
89:- **R-080 | Model layers** — станок local: :5001 generation 3B q4 ~5.6 tok/s (deep scenes only, raised on demand), :5002 BGE-M3 dim 1024 resident ~2.4 GB, lemmatizer pymorphy3 ~100 MB; external (swappable slots): Ткач/Редактор prose, deep-parse cheap call, Паганель large external LLM on owner key (UI card). Three presets, default local; config requirements per R-010. Source: DOCS/02-ARCHITECTURE.md:97–121. Status: PLAN.
90:- **R-081 | Three DBs + one-writer rule** — «три хозяина — три базы»: base.db (developer, build-time), literary.db (world мастерская; Гефест + оседание through Цензор), world(name).db (game; engine + player). Inside world(name).db TNS35 writer rule: one table = one writer; Forge touches only places, routes, world_meta; runtime writes the other 19 tables. Source: DOCS/02-ARCHITECTURE.md:125–139. Status: PLAN.
92:- **R-083 | Big Six replacement table** — TNS45 Big Six → TNS65: Драматург → Селектор; Актёр → voice card + bank of replicas / Ткач; Проверяющий → TS-filters, dictionary, mechanics; Стилист → microstyle + modulation / Ткач; Цензор → dictionary (double: turn + варка); Хронист → DB triggers, event sourcing; 6 LLM calls (≈5 min) → hybrid: 0 (рутина) or 1 (пик). Cut (не переезжает): narrative-bootstrapper, story-planner, director-loop, villain-manager, user-agent, researcher-agent, crafter-agent (open), Библия as entity, wiki-mechanics, Юбилей, cross-world-bus, feature-flags, dead intelligence/*. Source: DOCS/02-ARCHITECTURE.md:159–178. Status: PLAN.
98:- **R-089 | Pause ladder table (04)** — stage 1 ≥10 min (light, mechanics only), stage 2 >1 h (more complex ковка), stage 3 >3 h (heavy: new NPC elaboration, deep заготовки), Night: silence >8 h after chapter end (full варка, next-chapter пробуждение); stages cumulative. Source: DOCS/04-WORKSHOP.md:17–30. Status: PLAN.
99:- **R-090 | Forge queue + заготовки (04)** — resumable steps, continue from stop point; priorities 1–4 per R-038; near-need rule; demand 2–5/day; заготовка kinds: Паганель recon, new NPC, existing collisions, location descriptions, peak scenes, neutral пробуждение; review/censor before sleep; exception = instant book/bank characters. Source: DOCS/04-WORKSHOP.md:34–57. Status: PLAN.
100:- **R-091 | Гефест products + two доработки (04)** — products list incl. полотно тайн, voices/styles, epoch reference, пачка доковка (stage 3); fb2 insert detail (XML → metadata + body to chunker); Цензор при ковка at output; bank cleaned once. Source: DOCS/04-WORKSHOP.md:73–81. Status: PLAN.
101:- **R-092 | Паганель/Пифия tables (04)** — Паганель modes table with triggers and `edge_of_atlas`; ring/corridor; output schema; draft→baked; budgets ~10 calls/ring, ~3 recon; card toggles. Пифия: two floors (workshop full run / scene mechanics-only), three limits, гороскоп forged by Гефест. Source: DOCS/04-WORKSHOP.md:103–135. Status: PLAN.
104:- **R-095 | DB rights full table (05)** — 12 operations × 3 bases: build writes base.db; world-birth seed writes literary.db; анкета/creation writes world db (player); живой ход writes world db, reads others; player replicas/book edits/likes write world db; Гефест writes literary.db (through Цензор); оседание writes literary.db (trust levels); Паганель writes world db places/routes, never literary; fate vectors/доковка NPC write world db offline-events; пробуждение writes world db; night anchor drift reads all; Редактор+Цензор writes world db (player side). Source: DOCS/05-DATABASES.md:63–82. Status: PLAN.
106:- **R-097 | Пачка + доковка (05)** — card content: psychotype, estate, archetype, voice, looks; no backstory through second обращение; secret not set at birth. Use: binder-tag search (geography, estate, sex) → mechanical substitution, declension by card. Доковка: no fit → workshop order (Forge stage-3 pause) by required dramatic arc + Пифия score; card to world(name).db пачка; never forge new cards in the live turn. Source: DOCS/05-DATABASES.md:117–127. Status: PLAN.
110:- **R-101 | Role requirements table (06)** — lemmatizer (code), Ткач/Редактор (model, swappable slot), deep parse (external slot or local станок) with per-role requirements per R-008; presets and insurance per R-010; model manager lifecycle per R-011. Source: DOCS/06-MODELS-AND-SEED.md:7–23. Status: PLAN.
122:- **R-113 | Stage order 0–7 with criteria (08)** — 0 docs closure (T3–T9); 1 core+data (schemas by TNS35 contracts, base.db loader+vector counter, world recipe+анкета+пачка, literary.db move+seed load, facade :8000 + Telegram bridge + web WSS/cloudflared, event sourcing); 2 vertical live-turn slice (conveyor, Челнок, minimal Пила + Селектор stub, Ткач slot+insurance, binder, RU pack, streaming underlay, confirmed-only commit); 3 мастерская (pause timer+queue, Гефест+fb2+Цензор при варке, оседание conveyor, пробуждение+deep parse, fate vectors+offline commits); 4 seed+packs (bake steps; run by owner распоряжение); 5 Паганель/Пифия/мир-антагонист/сценарная рамка; 6 book+UI (утро главы, Редактор+Цензор, «Моя книга», анкета/заявка/death/replay/эпилог, лайк/дизлайк, admin zone); 7 full simulation heritage. Parallel to stage 0 only vertical slices of stage 2; canon source untouched until draft approved. Source: DOCS/08-DEVELOPMENT-PLAN.md:22–166. Status: PLAN.
